+## Get help
+
+1. Open **Settings → Help**, choose **Support tickets**, then **New ticket**.
+2. Choose a category, enter a **Subject** and **Message**, and select **Send ticket**. For **Raise call limit**, enter the number of simultaneous calls you need and why. For **Call me back**, you can include a callback number and a preferred time with its time zone.
+3. Open **My tickets** and select the subject to read the thread. **Waiting on customer** means support is waiting for your reply. Use **Send reply**, **Mark solved** or **Reply and reopen** as appropriate.
+
+Owners and Admins can see their organisation’s tickets. A Member sees only the tickets they opened. Support aims to reply within 48 hours, including weekends. If a ticket changed, choose **Refresh ticket** before editing. If a submission could not be confirmed and **Retry same request** appears, use that button to retry the same change.
+
 ## Profile and email preferences

 In **Settings → Profile**, use **Edit** beside the account name, then **Save**. Personal profile details and the organisation name are separate; use [Team](/guides/business/team) for organisation management.
